        <groundspeak:log id="616105963">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-08T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1565005">Takin it Easy</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP672 Westlock

Posted: N54° 09.395 W113° 50.622

GPSr: N54° 09.396 W113° 50.622&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lots of highway construction around Westlock today but things were pretty quiet at the cap GZ.  The traffic island grass was freshly cut and that should have led to a quick find but we just could not spot it.  We pulled out the Coolcat21 context shot and stood where the photo appeared to be taken. I took one step back and m foot hit the cap.  Nice!  The grass still obscured the cap really well even cut short.  Thanks for the cap OFTH!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="506014268">
          <groundspeak:date>2015-05-24T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="836983">Coolcat21</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP672 – Westlock

Posted: N54° 09.395' W113° 50.622'

My GPSr: N54° 09.396' W113° 50.624'&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s been a while since I’ve been to Westlock, and come to think of it the visits have only been for caching. Well, today I had capping on the brain instead and said cap was found quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This cap is located in an “island” of grass bordered one three sides by roads. I arrived as a landscaper was working discussing things with a home owner on the front lawn. They just might have thought a zombie-apocalypse may have begun because this guy was suddenly walking around seemingly aimlessly on that island of grass. In fact, I was saying “Argh, argh” in my head for the first couple of minutes, because I wasn't finding the cap but suddenly there it was, plain as day in front of me. Sheesh.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I took the required pics and then returned to the car, dragging my right leg on the ground the whole way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the cap!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
